      "writtenOn": "2026-07-21T13:06:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Implemented your suggestion as a separate cl: aosp/4187056\n\n\u003e  It seems we can: the host\u0027s pkvm_pasid_teardown() could easily use info-\u003edomain-\u003epgd?\n\nI did not implement this part and kept the teardown path derive the pgd from PASID. info-\u003edomain-\u003epgd is the default domain for the device and might not be the same for individual PAISDs(in the case of non-zeor PASIDs) for that device. So we need to derive the pgd from PASID entry in host as well to pass it to pkvm. We don\u0027t use non-zero PASIDS now and reject requests for non-zero PASIDS, but I feel keeping it as it is now would be better.\n\nSince the goal was to remove domain life management from cache-tag helper function, I focussed on that and we have the domain active through the life time of an active entry.\n\nPlease let me know if this is fine with you.",
      "parentUuid": "a3b01aec_d3c121b8",
      "revId": "21eb05d165ce6a9df3a6b06e5184ebaf8905773a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
